    "body": "\n\n## Overview\n\nOn CPUs, DeepSeek-V4 raises `KeyError: 'c1a'` at the first decode step, since #56228. Every release from v0.30.0 to v0.33.0 is affected. The CPU `build_tile_scheduler` override omits the `c1a` and `c2a` keys that the shared sparse-SWA metadata builder reads. This PR returns them with the sentinel `None`, as the base builder does, and adds a regression test. Fixes #65364.\n\n## Claims\n\n- DeepSeek-V4 on CPU decodes again: a decode step through `DeepseekV4CPUSparseSWAMetadataBuilder.build()` no longer raises `KeyError: 'c1a'`.\n- The new test fails on main with exactly that error and passes with this change.\n- The CPU kernel CI step now also triggers on `vllm/models/deepseek_v4/cpu/` and `vllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/sparse_swa.py`, so a future change on either side runs the test.\n\n## Validation\n\n**Unit test** (`tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v4_cpu_kernels.py`), on main `66360a5cd0`:\n\n```\n# main (this PR's vllm/ changes reverted)\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v4_cpu_kernels.py::test_cpu_swa_builder_decode_step_reads_every_layer_type -v\nE       KeyError: 'c1a'\nvllm/v1/attention/backends/mla/sparse_swa.py:790: KeyError\nFAILED ...::test_cpu_swa_builder_decode_step_reads_every_layer_type\n\n# this PR\nPASSED ...::test_cpu_swa_builder_decode_step_reads_every_layer_type\n.venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/kernels/test_deepseek_v4_cpu_kernels.py -q\n59 passed, 2 warnings in 42.57s\n```\n\n**End to end** on 2× AMD EPYC 9454 (2 NUMA nodes). DeepSeek-V4-Flash config with dummy weights: `load_format=\"dummy\"`, `hf_overrides={\"num_hidden_layers\": 4, \"num_nextn_predict_layers\": 0, \"quantization_config\": None}`, `dtype=bfloat16`, `--enforce-eager`.\n\n| Run | main `66360a5cd0` | this PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| TP1, `CpuPlatform` | `KeyError: 'c1a'` at the first decode step | decodes (TP1, checked with the same setup on `6d01893483`) |\n| TP1, `ZenCpuPlatform` | `KeyError: 'c1a'` at the first decode step (`sparse